  "findings": "The controlling 2026–2027 chart confirms 60 EC each year, the zero-credit BRIDGE, the seven-course year-three option pool and a required 12 EC thesis. The official thesis and practical records establish the 120 EC and two-pass threshold and the alternative 5.5 practical thresholds. The UCR options provide a viable mathematics-to-models sequence with applied econometrics and machine learning. The consumer pathway shifts five courses toward markets, primary customer research and business use of AI. Both preserve statistical and ethical foundations. Neither offers the full econometrics sequence, stand-alone multivariate statistics or a technical fairness and privacy sequence. Current descriptions establish genuine investment-appraisal overlap between Finance I and UCR accounting and finance, while VU’s asset-pricing and portfolio material extends beyond that overlap. Both schedules meet the current term and prerequisite constraints, with 37.5 EC of course differences in each direction and optional independent research outside the schedule.",
